From 1f5c88c9eeffda750cc8dc38380e8eed6f945564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:22:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 311/350] Unified: a part linked from an assembly in another
 file is still a part of its own file

doc.RootObjects leaves out an object that an object of another document
uses: once the assembly linked the connecting rod, "Make Drawing" in the
rod's file said there was no part to draw (engine field test 0.7.3), and
dragging, push/pull, export and the parts not in an assembly missed it
too. UnifiedFiles.root_objects(doc): what nothing in the same document
uses.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestUnifiedFiles

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Mod/Unified/MagnetDragGui.py    |  3 ++-
 src/Mod/Unified/PartsShelf.py       |  3 ++-
